p95 is read from the run's own demo block. Reduce latency; or the owner may log
'# <date> [waiver] p95_latency_seconds <demo.generated_at> <p95> <ticket> <why>'
in budgets.toml. It covers that one run only, and goes in its own commit: a waiver
added in the same change as code fails 'new exemptions' in check_invariants.

STOP. Do not edit budgets.toml to make this pass.

A budget exceeded means one of two things:
  1. The change is carrying complexity it does not need -> simplify it.
  2. The product genuinely outgrew the budget -> stop and ask the human,
     who will raise it in a separate commit with a written reason.

Raising a limit yourself defeats the only mechanism protecting this
project from the failure mode it was built to avoid.

